<title>JAPAN: Tietmeyer sees US not wanting 'stronger' dlr--Jiji.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer sees US not wanting 'stronger' dlr--Jiji.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Sunday in Washington that he thinks the United States does not want a &quot;stronger&quot; dollar, Japanese news agency Jiji reported.</p>
<p>Jiji quoted Tietmeyer as telling some reporters after the Group of Seven (G7) meeting: &quot;I think the U.S. wants a strong dollar, but not a stronger one.&quot;</p>
<p>Tietmeyer also said: &quot;We do not want a weak yen, but a strong yen.&quot;</p>
<p>Tietmeyer's remarks helped push the dollar down from morning peaks of 127.10 yen and 1.7395 marks.</p>
</text>
